Cutoff Sequence
The cutoff signal, received from the vehicle programmer, de-energizes the engine-control valve causing it to close. This closure vents the open side and pressurizes the closing side of the main propellant-valve actuators. By proper orificing of the helium lines, the main oxidizer valve is made to close faster than the main fuel valve, to ensure a fuel-rich cutoff. The valve closure causes engine thrust to decay. The fuel bleed valve opens after venting of the helium pressure in its actuator.
